  |CN	| 2020-02-05 | 8.2.1.1 | Incremental changes to to 8.2.1.0 | Compiled in MODGEN 12.1.1.0 using VS2015

					- Table tMeasuredSrYouthBMI, aka "Youth BMI distribution and average (self-reported or measured) by sex, age, year" was introduced.
					- Table tMeasuredSrAdultBMI, aka "Adult BMI distribution and average (self-reported or measured) by sex, age, year" was introduced.  
					- Table tBMIcat set to be decomissioned, hence its long name "BMI distribution (decomission forthcoming - should instead use table  BMI distribution and average (self-reported or measured) by sex, age, year )"
					- WHO_cutoffs[][][AGE_YOUTH_MONTH][]  was only used with third dimension set to 0 (i.e. WHO_cutoffs[][][0][] ).  Now it is used with third dimension set to AgeYouthMonthSimu. 
 					  No visible change to outputs since AgeYouthMonthSimu=0 in default scenario
					- BMI for youth is now constrained by new parameter YouthBmiBounds.  It was previously constrained by COERCE(BMI_RANGE, ...), i.e. [12,55], which was designed with adults in mind.
                                          It turns out that [12,55] also seems OK for children so this is the default settings of YouthBmiBounds.  
					- States  bmi4cat_measured_start     , bmi4cat_measured     , gBMImeasured were removed so that one is more likely to pick the proper PHAC counterparts in the future
					  that is bmi4cat_measured_start_PHAC, bmi4cat_measured_PHAC, gBMImeasured_PHAC.

