  |CN   | 2019-05-30 | 8.2.0.1 | Incremental changes to 8.2.0.0 (modgen 12) | Compiled in MODGEN 12.1.1.0 using VS2015

						MPoRT  

						- The introduction of MPoRT (V1 and mostly V2) in POHEM is the main purpose of this version.
						- MPoRT V1 involves two parameters: MportV1Coeffients and  MportV1MinOneYearSuvival
						- MPoRT V2 involves 6 splines (thus 6*2 parameters from splines) with respect to age, pack years, number of drinks, MET, BMI, Cdn resident percent
						- MPoRT V2 also involves 4 other parameters for a grand total of 16 parameters.
                           Those 4 non-spline parameters are MportV2Baseline, MportV2MainTermsMeans, MportV2MainTermsCoefficients, MportV2InteractionCoefficients 
						- MPoRT has a few loose ends and has not been fully tested.  The ability to run MPoRT has thus been disabled.

						Miscellaneous (sprung by introduction of MPoRT in POHEM)

						- A new StartPop file has been created.
						- Parameter MortalityEngine now replaces parameter NphsMortality.
						- MET from leasure time physical activity is now modeled and involves parameters MetDistribution and MetCorrelation.
						- Time since immigration  is now modeled and involves parameters ImmigrationTimingAge, ImmigrationTimingYear and ImmigrationTimingInteractionYearAge.
						- Time since quit smoking is now modeled and involves parameter TimeSinceQuitDistribution (and change to StartPop file).
						- Table tPop_Count has been changed to also show death counts and death hazard rates.
   
  
  |DH   | 2019-05-21 | 8.2.0.0 | Incremental changes to 8.2.0.0 to convert to modgen 12 | Compiled in MODGEN 12.1.1.0 using VS2015

						This is the first version of POHEM compiled with MODGEN 12.

						- Hook order/priority are now explicitly specified in order to avoid warnings in modgen 12.
						- Modgen 12 did not like parameter pRF_INTERVENTION_ALLOW_CHANGE_IN_BMI_IN_START_YEAR_TO_CHANGE_HUI_IN_START_YEAR.
						  It was therefore given a shorter name: pRF_INTERVENTION_ALLOW_CHANGE_IN_BMI_START_YEAR_TO_CHANGE_HUI. 
						- POHEM 8200 (modgen12) gave the same results as POHEM 8200 (modgen11)- after sorting out the hook order.  


  |CN,DH| 2019-05-13 | 8.2.0.0 | Incremental changes to 8.1.3.0 | Compiled in MODGEN 11.7.3.0 using VS2010

						This could be the last version of POHEM compiled with MODGEN 11.

						- Stroke/SPoRt module was removed. It will be replaced by forthcoming CVDPoRt
						- Parameter pDisease was reduced to only show things that are actually modeled in POHEM.  So Diabetes, CAD-AMI, OA and OA drug side effect were kept. Everything else (e.g. lung cancer) is gone.
						- Corrected a bug that impacted who was subject to the alteration of the diabetes status read in from the StartPop file.
						- Removed province dimension in table tDiseaseEvents which made it very large.
						- DPoRT was calibrated to agree with CCDSS diabetes prevalence.
						- Parameter MinLife (Minimum number of years of life) was introduced.  It is the companion of MaxLife (Maximum number of years of life) which has been around for ever.  
						  MinLife may be useful for debugging but has otherwise no real application.

 
  |CN,DH| 2019-04-01 | 8.1.3.0 | Incremental changes to 8.1.2.2 | Compiled in MODGEN 11.7.3.0 using VS2010

						CUBIC SPLINES
						- The function CubicSpline was introduced.  It should ease the implementation of cubic spline in the future. 

						BMI
						- Parameter BuiltInBmiAlterationSpecs was introduced to nudge the BMI model closer to the SR BMI observed in CCHS for years up to 2016.

						DIABETES
						- Parameter DportAlterationSpecs was introduced to alter the risk of diabetes according to DPoRT.  Alteration may be made by sex and age group to align with CCDSS prevalence targets.
						- Parameter DportAlterationSpecsAppliesToDiabetesPrevalenceFixSR indicates if the alterations should also be applied in DPoRTish10YearProb which is used
						  in the new way to tamper with diabetes read in from StartPop (this approach was introduced in POHEM 8.1.2.2).
						- Parameter DiabetesPrevalenceTarget2001 now uses finer age groups.  The target is synthetic and was obtained using raking on known margins (see Technical Notes for 8130).
						- Parameters DiabetesInitialAlterationPopulationScope and DiabetesInitialAlterationYearScope were introduced to specify whom is subject to tampering of their diabetes read in from StartPop 
						- The elevated risk of mortality due to diabetes was re-implemented using the new CubicSpline function.  A bug with previous spline implementation was found (see Technical Notes for 8130).
						  - The new implementation requires the parameters DiabetesMortalityRelRiskAgeSplineLocationCoef  and DiabetesMortalityRelRiskAgeSplineCompanion  for the age  spline.
						  - The new implementation requires the parameters DiabetesMortalityRelRiskYearSplineLocationCoef and DiabetesMortalityRelRiskYearSplineCompanion for the year spline.
						  - The new implementation led to a leaner version of pDiabetes_RR_Mortality as some of its former content moved to the cubic spline parameters mentioned above.  
						  - Parameter pDB_RR_Max_Year was removed and its content was moved to the cubic spline parameters mentioned above.
						- Another bug for the elevated risk of mortality due to diabetes was found and corrected (see Technical Notes for 8130).  
						
						TABLES
						- Table tDiseaseEventsDiab uses a different age group.

  | CN  | 2019-01-24 | 8.1.2.2 | Incremental changes to 8.1.2.1 | Compiled in MODGEN 11.7.3.0 using VS2010
					
                      This implements an alternative way to tamper with diabetes read in from StartPop. This involves new parameters DiabetesPrevalenceTarget2001 and WeightForUnderlyingDPoRTishUniform.
					  There is another new parameter called TimeHorizonForDport which specifies the time horizon for which POHEM computes the risk of diabetes before converting it to annual hazard.
					  This time horizon used to be hard-coded to 10.  It is set to 2 in the default scenario. 
					  POHEM 8.1.2.2 reproduces results from POHEM 8.1.2.1.

  | CN  | 2019-01-16 | 8.1.2.1 | Incremental changes to 8.1.2.0 | Compiled in MODGEN 11.7.3.0 using VS2010
					
                      The main raison d’être of 8.1.2.1 is to merge 8.1.2.0 with 8.0.1.2-ish (aka 8.0.2.0 though no such version officially exists) which is a branch out of 8.0.1.2 that introduced/implemented "metformin".  
					  In addition, the PreSimulation code of BMIyouth.mpp was re-structured to ease its re-use for other application foreseen later (alternative to DiabetesPrevalenceStartCheck).  
					  POHEM 8.1.2.1 reproduces results from  POHEM 8.1.2.0 and  POHEM 8.0.1.2-ish. 

  | CN  | 2019-01-14 | 8.1.2.0 | Incremental changes to 8.1.1.0 | Compiled in MODGEN 11.7.3.0 using VS2010
					
                       The purpose of 8.1.2.0 is to strip veterans from 8.1.1.0.  
					   POHEM 8.1.2.0 replicates the results of 8.0.1.2 (the pre-veteran version of POHEM) but retains some functionality introduced along the way and code restructuring.
                                 1. veterans.mpp module was removed
								 2. all parameters related to veterans (including model_generated) were removed and code that was using them was removed or altered
								 3. cNewVeterans was removed from classification cPopulationSource
								 4. POHEM 8.1.2.0 uses the StartPop file from POHEM 8.0.1.2 and cDb_Veteran removed from DB_FIELDS

  |CN	| 2018-04-09 | 8.1.1.0 This is the second version of POHEM-veteran. 
                          The following parameters were introduced or modified.
                                 1. RakeInYoungVeteran tells whether the parameter pVeterans needs to be raked (e.g. new 17 year old veterans in 2022 to be dismissed or to be seen as new 20 year old veterans in 2025).
						 	 	 2. The mortality hazard of Regular Force Veterans is altered through the relative risk parameter pVeteranMortRate.
								 3. ProbabilityVacClient contains the probability that a veteran is a client of Veteran Affairs Canada (VAC) as a function of HUI group, age group and sex.
								 4. A parameter trio was introduced: NewVeteranDonorDef, NewVeteranDonorConditionField and NewVeteranDonorConditionRange. 
								    They allow the user to say what is an acceptable donor for the creation a new veteran in the future.
									Also, the modgen code is now set up to use, if needed, an expanded donor pool which ignores the veteran status (see model_generated parameter mgCumStartPopWeightVeteransOfAllKinds).
								 5. A parameter trio was introduced: pStartPopReweightDefinitionFields, pStartPopReweightDefinitionBounds, pStartPopReweightMultiplier.
								    They allow one to modify the survey weights of some respondents on the StartPop file.
								    The new trio replaces the now defunct parameter duo pStartPopRestrictionField and pStartPopRestrictionBounds.
								 6. Removed some old/unused parameters: ZSCORE, RandomShuffleSeed, EvaluateCauseSpecificSurvival.

                          The following tables were introduced or modified. 
                                 1. The model shipped to Veteran Affairs Canada (VAC) only show the following 4 tables (TG_NonVeteran_Tables hidden in VAC's version of POHEM 8110).
									A) tPopulation_Veteran --> Population and mortality by sex, age, year and veteran status
									B) tVaria_Veteran_Lean --> Several things (e.g. proportion obese) by sex, veteran status, age and year
								    C) tPopulation_Start_Veteran --> Population by year created, age created, sex and veteran status
									D) tHui_3Categories_Veteran_Client --> Counts by HUI category, sex, veteran status, age and year
								 2. Introduced some utility tables.
								    A) tStart_Pop_AgeSexVet_Original_Distribution and tStart_Pop_AgeSexVet_Altered_Distribution show the (age, sex, veteran status) distribution of respondents before and after the alteration of survey weights.
									B) tStart_Pop_Sex, tStart_Pop_Bmi, tStart_Pop_Age, tStart_Pop_Veteran_Status, tStart_Pop_Survey_Weight spit out micro data from the StartPop file.  Those tables are commented out.
									C) tStart_Pop_Donor_Used_Count shows how often a given record is used to initialise an actor. The table is commented out.

                          A few changes were made to parameter groups and table groups, mostly to first show things relevant to Veteran Affairs Canada (VAC).
								 
  |CN	| 2017-04-13 | 8.1.0.0 This is the first version of POHEM-veteran.  The following parameters were introduced or modified.
                                 1. pVeterans [YEARS][SEX][VETERAN2][LIFE] gives the actual and projected number of releases from regular forces or reserve forces.
						 	 	 2. Created a new StartPop file that contains dummy information for veteran status.
								 3. pNewArrivalsControl allows for all 16 possible ways to run the model (e.g. StartPop and future veterans but not future births nor future immigrants).
								 4. It is now possible to subset the StartPop file on the fly (e.g. only males) through two new parameters pStartPopReweightDefinitionFields and pStartPopReweightDefinitionBounds.
								 5. The parameter AimAtAllFutureImmigrants allows one to simulate new immigrants according to the parameter pImmig (TRUE) or an altered version thereof (FALSE). 
								    The latter setting corresponds to what POHEM 8012 did.
								 6. The parameter AimAtAllFutureYoungAdults allows one to scope the future young adults (20 year old) in the future.  
								    If set to TRUE, new young adults are simulated to conceptually align with to the census definition (20 year old with a pulse).  
									If set to FALSE, POHEM tries to conceptually align with the CCHS population definition (e.g. exclude people in the army turning age 20 in year 2005).  
									The FALSE setting corresponds to what POHEM 8012 did.
								 7. The parameter UseNewUnduplicationMethod offers a slightly different way to unduplicate population sources (e.g. new birth and new immigrants). 
								    The FALSE setting corresponds to what POHEM 8012 did.
								 8. The parameter ForceInitialisationToNonVeteran  , when set to TRUE, allows the user to set veteran   status to "not veteran  " after a donor from CCHS was selected (does not impact the donor selection process itself).
								 9. The parameter ForceInitialisationToNonImmigrant, when set to TRUE, allows the user to set immigrant status to "not immigrant" after a donor from CCHS was selected (does not impact the donor selection process itself).
							   A few tables were also created to tabulate veterans : tPop_Count_Veteran, tPopulation_Province_Veteran, tPopulation_Start_Veteran

